From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 08:40:00 +0200
Subject: 0024: let horizontal nav tab extensions render before the object loads

A `console.tab/horizontalNav` extension is matched against the *live
object* (`referenceFor(props.obj.data)`), while core's own tabs come from
the static `pages` array and render immediately. So a plugin's tab can
only appear once that object's watch resolves - seconds later on a busy
cluster, since a details page mounted while API discovery is in flight
dispatches no watch at all until discovery settles (`useModelsLoaded`
latches per component instance).

For an ordinary added tab that is a cosmetic pop-in. For the flag-gated
Pod and Node Terminal tabs (0019, 0020) it is a hole: core drops its own
tab as soon as the plugin's `console.flag` handler resolves - which it
does in milliseconds, off a single `config.json` fetch - but the
plugin's replacement can't appear until the object lands, so the details
page shows *no* Terminal tab in between.

The route already knows which kind it is rendering, so pass that model's
reference down from DetailsPage and use it to match tab extensions while
`obj.data` is still in flight. The tab *contents* are unaffected: they
stay behind HorizontalNav's own StatusBox, so an extension's component is
still only mounted once the object is really there.

`pagesFor` pages (Node details) contribute no tabs at all until the
object loads, since the callback needs the object to decide - e.g.
`isWindowsNode(node)`. Extension tabs must not be joined onto that empty
list, or a Node details page would briefly show a tab bar holding nothing
but the plugin's Terminal tab, so they are added only once core has
contributed its own.
